===== FILE: README.md =====
# Orion

Orion is an ownerless randomness protocol for Arc. A contract asks for a random number, and the number comes from the public drand beacon (network `evmnet`). The beacon signature is verified onchain, so nobody can predict or choose the result. Anyone can run a relayer bot to deliver the signatures and earn the USDC reward attached to each request.

The contracts are named `RandomnessHub`, `RandomnessConsumer` and so on. Deployed contract names cannot change, so the code keeps them.

Status: tested on Arc Testnet only. Not audited. Do not use with real funds.

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `contracts/RandomnessHub.sol` | The protocol: requests, signature check, rewards, callbacks |
| `contracts/IRandomnessHub.sol` | Interface for integrators |
| `contracts/RandomnessConsumer.sol` | Base contract your app inherits |
| `contracts/RandomnessDemo.sol` | Minimal example consumer |
| `contracts/test/` | Foundry tests and 18 real drand rounds |
| `scripts/relayer.ts` | Relayer bot |
| `scripts/monitor.ts` | Read-only health report |
| `scripts/live-test.ts` | End-to-end test on Arc Testnet |
| `docs/` | Integration guide, process description, advantages, launch checklist, reports |

## Setup

Requirements: [Bun](https://bun.sh) and [Foundry](https://getfoundry.sh).

```bash
bun install
forge install foundry-rs/forge-std
forge build
forge test
```

`forge install` puts `forge-std` in `lib/`, which `remappings.txt` expects.

## Environment variables

Set these in a `.env` file. Never commit it.

- `VITE_RANDOMNESS_HUB_ADDRESS`: address of the deployed hub. Needed by the scripts.
- `VITE_RANDOMNESS_DEMO_ADDRESS`: address of the demo consumer. Needed by the live test.
- `RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY`: key of a dedicated, funded wallet for the relayer and the live test.
- `RPC_URL_Arc_Testnet`: optional, your own RPC endpoint. Without it the scripts use the public RPC.
- `RELAYER_LOOKBACK`: optional, how many recent requests the relayer checks on start (default 300).
- `RELAYER_MIN_REWARD_WEI`: optional, the relayer skips requests that pay less than this.

## Commands

```bash
bun run relayer               # run the relayer (add -- --once or -- --dry-run)
bun run monitor               # health report (add -- --watch)
bun run test:live             # end-to-end test on Arc Testnet
```

